	<language_code>eng</language_code>
	<description>Arguably Patricia Highsmith's finest, &lt;em&gt;The Price of Salt&lt;/em&gt; is story of Therese Belivet, a stage designer trapped in a department-store day job, whose salvation arrives one day in the form of Carol Aird, an alluring suburban housewife in the throes of a divorce. They fall in love and set out across the United States, pursued by a private investigator who eventually blackmails Carol into a choice between her daughter and her lover. With this reissue, &lt;em&gt;The Price of Salt&lt;/em&gt; may finally be recognized as a major twentieth-century American novel.</description>
